From ea3f6690e8baa12a8a7b81fdb418690738fa75d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:11:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 352/353] DOS-PORT: patch 0352 -- retire the AUDIOPRB
 audio-cost timings (ags side)

Removes the S7 / S7-GUS "TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC" family's engine half: the audio_core
poll windows (slots_us / pump_us, ags 0059 with 0061's sink fold), the folds of SDL's
OPL3 regwrite / GUS getstate / GUS voice x5 / GUS upload snapshots (0062, 0069, 0070,
0073), the midi_sched_tick call-site bracket (0071), the gus_sink_prepare_song bracket
(0072), 0218's hint latch in engine_init_audio, and quit.cpp's "DOS-PORT audioprb" dump
(including the one "audioprb timing=off total_calls=" line every run printed).

All of it has been off by default since ags 0218 / SDL 0199 (SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_DIAG_TIMING);
no gate scorer, capture scorer or ratchet check reads it; the investigation it served
(S7: the GUS 6.89 s slot-poll outlier) concluded. The SDL half (0141, 0145-0147, 0199) is
retired by a separate patches/SDL patch. PLAN-NEXT step 1b.
